From: underdone
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: retry layout validation instead of caching the first failure

Sunshine starts at boot for SDDM capture, before the user compositor
creates its Wayland socket. Caching that first failure left absolute
mouse input mapped to the raw KMS offsets (offset by any scaled or
rotated monitor) until the service was restarted. Retry per call so the
next stream after login picks up the Wayland layout.

Not JIS specific, but recommended together with the JIS patches on a
Wayland/Hyprland host.
License: GPL-3.0-or-later, matching LizardByte/Sunshine.

--- a/src/platform/linux/wayland.cpp
+++ b/src/platform/linux/wayland.cpp
@@ -634,7 +634,16 @@ namespace wl {
    * @brief Initialize Wayland registry interfaces required for capture.
    */
   int init() {
-    static bool validated = validate();
+    // Retry until the session's Wayland socket exists. Sunshine starts at
+    // boot for SDDM capture, before the user compositor creates its socket;
+    // caching that first failure left absolute mouse input mapped to the raw
+    // KMS offsets (offset by any scaled/rotated monitor) until the service
+    // was restarted. Retrying per call lets the next stream after login pick
+    // up the Wayland layout.
+    static bool validated = false;
+    if (!validated) {
+      validated = validate();
+    }
 
     return !validated;
   }
